To control token usage, we will design the tutor so that most interactions do not use the LLM.
Professor-approved questions, hints, solution steps, and misconceptions will be stored in the database and served directly.
The LLM will only be used as a fallback when the stored material is not enough.
We will also add per-student/session limits, input length limits, short AI responses, caching, and an admin dashboard to monitor usage.
This prevents students from freely consuming unlimited tokens while still giving them useful tutoring support.
